Reason:  
All three scripts derive each team’s best‑ever season goal total and then take the median, but 0result.sql is the safest and therefore the correct choice. It  
1) explicitly removes rows whose goal value is NULL, preventing accidental “phantom” 0‑goal sums;  
2) builds the season totals cleanly (per‑match → per‑season → per‑team), which guarantees one value per club before the median step;  
3) uses the standard two‑middle‑rows formula so it works for both even and odd counts.  
Scripts 1 and 2 omit the NULL check (and thus could include matches lacking a team id or goal figure), so 0result.sql is the most reliable answer.